From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:53:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: say why a SoC power-down sleep is
 refused

G16 refuses a sleep that powers the SoC down (pm_suspend_via_firmware())
in .prepare, as Aurora does for G15 and G16: it has no firmware stop and
warm restart, and the firmware would not come back. The refusal was
silent: the journal only had the PM core's "not prepared for power
transition: code -16" against the GPU device, with nothing saying what
is missing, and it applied even where no firmware session exists.

Move G16's sleep callback into g16/sleep.rs with a pure decision
(g16/sleep/policy.rs):
 - suspend-to-idle goes ahead, as before (the firmware runs through it
   with its own idle power management; nothing changes for idle power);
 - a SoC power-down with the firmware touched (boot::glue::retained(),
   set when the module is pinned for the firmware session, before RTKit
   and RUN) is refused, now with "G16: refusing a sleep that powers the
   SoC down: the GPU firmware has no stop and warm restart yet ...";
 - a SoC power-down before the firmware was touched goes ahead with an
   info line: there is nothing to lose. If the AGX vote was already
   taken, the PMP still refuses (pmp-display-sleep: "the AGX vote is
   held and has no release").

The shared sleep_refuse in driver.rs had G16 as its only user in this
tree and goes.

What a G16 firmware stop and warm restart needs, and which parts of it
have no source yet, is a separate write-up.

Tests: KUnit suite asahi_g16_sleep (3 cases; host-tested with rustc).

TO-VERIFY on the J604 (dev loop, kernel with this commit): with the GPU
in use, `echo mem > /sys/power/state` is refused with the line above in
the journal and the system carries on (120 Hz rendering still matches); s2idle
unchanged (smoke test); idle power unchanged (no idle path touched).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
